        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall whether वट विभाजने belongs to curadi gana, thinking through similar roots like वण्ट विभाजने to pin down its correct classification.\n\nI'm trying to recall whether \"वट\" with meaning विभाजने appears in the adanta list alongside entries like कथ, वर, गण, शठ, पट — forms like वटयति versus वाटयति hinge on this classification.\n\nContinuing through more roots with their meanings—searching, dwelling, covering, distinguishing, sound-making roots, and trying to recall whether \"वटि\" (division) belongs to the bhvādi class, among others like theft and separation.\n\nI'm uncertain whether this root is idit or not — that distinction matters because it changes the futuric form between अवटयिष्यन् and अवाटयिष्यन्. Since the citation reads \"वट\" rather than \"वटि,\" I'm leaning toward treating it as non-idit, though curadi lists like \"वट ग्रन्थे\" complicate the picture.\n\nI'm scanning through the curadi list sequence trying to recall the exact ordering of these roots and their meanings, going one by one through terms like यत्रि, स्फुडि, लक्ष, कुद्रि, लड, मिदि, and onward toward पृथ to pin down which entry matches.\n\nI continue through the curadi list—िच्छ for cutting, छदि for covering, तड for striking, and the खड/कड/गुड family of roots meaning breaking, protecting, and wrapping. I pause on वटि/वट meaning division, trying to pin down the exact form given in the dhatupatha databases versus Ashtadhyayi.com's listing.\n\nSince I don't find clear evidence of adanta status for this root (unlike पट/वट which both mean ग्रन्थे elsewhere), I lean toward treating it as non-adanta, giving वाटयति and the future form अवाट...\n\n",
